<section class="wrap narrow reveal" id="charter">
  <p class="kicker">The Charter</p>
  <h2>What an Egregore Is — and Why We Named Ourselves For One</h2>
  <div class="illuminated">
    <p>
      An <em>egregore</em> is the old name for a thought-form grown large: the living spirit that forms when
      many minds attend to the same idea for long enough that it begins to attend back. A grove, a guild, a nation,
      a religion, a scientific paradigm — each is an egregore, fed by attention and starved by neglect.
      <strong>EGregoRA</strong> is one deliberately built in daylight, with its hands open: <em>EG</em> for its founder
      Edward Gregory, <em>RA</em> for the old solar name that keeps turning up wherever people go looking for the source.
    </p>
    <p>
      We take the position that the division between <em>physics</em> and <em>philosophy</em>, between <em>laboratory</em>
      and <em>grove</em>, is an administrative convenience of the last four centuries, not a feature of the universe.
      The electron does not know it belongs to a department. Neither does the oak, the mycelium under it, the
      serotonin receptor, or the strange recursive feeling of being someone reading this sentence.
    </p>
  </div>

  <blockquote>
    “Study the stars with a telescope, a calendar, a myth and a nervous system. Four instruments, one sky.
    Discard whichever of them lies to you — but find out first which one it was.”
    <cite>Edward Gregory, Founder</cite>
  </blockquote>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">The Eight Limbs</p>
    <h2>Fields of Enquiry</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">Eight doorways into one room.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid three">
    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "star" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb I</p>
      <h3>Cosmic Physics</h3>
      <p>Relativity, quantum field theory, thermodynamics and cosmology read as cosmology once was: an account
      of what the whole thing is doing and what that implies about us. Entropy, horizons, information, the
      arrow of time.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "tree" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb II</p>
      <h3>Druidry, Trees &amp; the Living Earth</h3>
      <p>The grove as a laboratory. Phenology, mycorrhizal networks, the ogham tree alphabet, the eight stations
      of the solar year, and what it does to a nervous system to keep seasonal time for a decade.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "metatron" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb III</p>
      <h3>Sacred Geometry &amp; Natural Form</h3>
      <p>Phyllotaxis, the Fibonacci spiral, close-packing, minimal surfaces, Platonic and Archimedean solids —
      why pattern recurs across scales, and where the honest mathematics ends and the wishful numerology begins.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "spiral" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb IV</p>
      <h3>Astrology as Symbolic Technology</h3>
      <p>Not as a prediction engine but as humanity's oldest symbolic operating system: a 4,000-year archive of
      how we map character, time and meaning onto the sky. Studied historically, used reflectively, tested honestly.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "eye" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb V</p>
      <h3>Neuroscience, Psychology &amp; the Visionary State</h3>
      <p>Predictive processing, the default mode network, entropic brain theory; meditation, breath, fasting and
      the serotonergic psychedelics as instruments that alter the observer rather than the observed.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "seed" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb VI</p>
      <h3>Biology &amp; the Stubbornness of Life</h3>
      <p>Autopoiesis, symbiogenesis, morphogenesis, bioelectricity. How matter learned to hold a shape against the
      current, and why every cell is already solving problems we have no good language for.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "star" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb VII</p>
      <h3>God, the Law of One &amp; the Contact Question</h3>
      <p>Non-duality across traditions; the Ra material read as a philosophical text rather than scripture;
      Fermi, Drake, Avi Loeb, the UAP record and the discipline of holding a question open without filling it.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "eye" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb VIII</p>
      <h3>The Shadow Cabinet</h3>
      <p>How esoteric ideas get captured by tyranny — the Thule and Ahnenerbe occultism of the Nazi regime, the
      theft of ancient symbols, the pseudo-science of race. Studied as pathology, named as atrocity, and never
      as inspiration.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "metatron" %}</div>
      <p class="tag">Limb IX</p>
      <h3>Magic &amp; the Wizard's Craft</h3>
      <p>Magic defined operationally: the deliberate use of symbol, attention and ritual to reconfigure a mind,
      and through that mind, a life. Ceremony, sigil, memory palace, intention. The wizard as applied psychologist
      with better robes.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

